<.shell current={:filter_a_list}>
  <h1>Filter a list</h1>
  <p class="lead">The activity list: filters, a summary line, the table, and pages.</p>

  <div class="example">
    <.filter_bar
      for={sample_filters()}
      id="sample-filters"
      count="212 activities"
      clear="#"
      path_fn={fn _ -> "#" end}
      page={sample_filter_page()}
      onsubmit="return false"
    >
      <:search field={sample_filters()[:q]} />
      <:filter
        field={sample_filters()[:kind]}
        label="Kind"
        options={sample_kinds()}
        default="all"
      />
      <:filter
        field={sample_filters()[:when]}
        label="When"
        options={sample_whens()}
        default="all"
      />
    </.filter_bar>
    <div class="table-actions">
      <.button type="button">Add to group</.button>
      <.button type="button">Remove from group</.button>
    </div>
    <.activity_table
      id="sample-activities"
      rows={activities()}
      sort="date-"
      path_fn={fn _ -> "#" end}
      team={sample_team()}
    />
    <.pagination class="my-4" paginated={sample_page()} path_fn={fn _ -> "#" end} />
  </div>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      The <a href={page_path(:filter_bar)}>filter bar</a>
      sits above the table: a search box and a menu per filter. A menu that filters something turns blue.
    </li>
    <li>The line under it has the count and Clear filters, and which rows the page shows.</li>
    <li>
      Actions on ticked rows, such as Add to group, go in a <code>.table-actions</code>
      row under it, sized like the bar: 36px, small text, 44px on a touch screen.
    </li>
    <li>The column headers sort the table.</li>
    <li><a href={page_path(:pagination)}>Pagination</a> goes under the table, 50 rows a page.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="spec">
    In the app: <code>&lt;.activity_filter_table&gt;</code>. The bar is <code>&lt;.filter_bar&gt;</code>, and the table is <code>&lt;.activity_table&gt;</code>, shown here with made-up activities.
  </p>
</.shell>
